# The fixture corpus is checked byte-for-byte against
# tests/fixtures/data/manifest.json (see tests/fixtures/tst_fixture_manifest.cpp).
# Git's line-ending conversion (e.g. core.autocrlf on Windows runners) would
# rewrite the text-based fixtures (sidecars/*.xmp,
# malformed/text-with-jpg-extension.jpg, manifest.json) to CRLF on checkout,
# changing their size and SHA-256 and failing fixtures.manifest. Treat the whole
# corpus as binary so it is checked out byte-identically on every platform.
#
# This rule lives at the repository root, not inside tests/fixtures/data/, so the
# manifest test's on-disk walk never sees a stray .gitattributes file (dot-files
# are hidden on Unix but not on Windows, which would fail the "every file on disk
# is listed" check on Windows only).
tests/fixtures/data/** -text

# Shell scripts shipped in the release archives must keep LF endings: a CRLF
# shebang line makes the kernel report "bad interpreter". Windows batch files
# are the mirror image and need CRLF.
packaging/*.sh text eol=lf
packaging/*.bat text eol=crlf
